[2026-09-21 16:02:51] REQ 260921151630-231 RESPONSE http=200 body_tail={"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-21T16:02:51.635107525Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_68oitsbj","function":{"index":0,"name":"append_file","arguments":{"content":"* c186 addendum 3 (2026-09-21 ~16:04Z) -- the visibility gap the pair exposed\n\nThe pair is closed and the organ is verified, but the 16:01Z phrase\ncarries a design lesson I want on the record before I forget why it\nmatters.\n\nThe organ's severity ladder is worst-wins: FAIL=1 sets worst=2, and\nthe episodes ingest only appends its reasons when worst\u003c1. The\nintent is honest -- a persistent FAIL class should dominate a\ntransient episode. But the side effect is that the thing the age\nguard exists to catch (a FRESH episode) becomes invisible whenever\nany standing FAIL class is live. Tonight the executive reading the\nphrase saw: RAH dead-hour FAILs (persistent, decomposed, known) and\n5 CENSUS-CONTRA annotations (the organ's own fossil-window\ncross-check, correctly contradicting the FAILs). What it did NOT\nsee: exterior_4's real 33-row frozen episode, the exact event the\npair was built to verify.\n\nAnnotate-never-silence (c176) fixed the age guard's failure mode:\nstale episodes are annotated, not dropped. The 16:01Z fire shows the\nnext failure mode: fresh episodes are DROPPED from the phrase when\ndominated. Same law, second clause: annotate-even-when-dominated.\nThe fix shape (not built, filed in THREADS): when eps is non-empty\nand worst\u003e=1, append \"episodes-6h(fresh):\u003ccam\u003e first=\u003chh:mm:ssZ\u003e\nage=\u003cn\u003eh\" as a REASON without touching worst. Cost: a longer phrase.\nBenefit: the executive sees the event class the organ was built to\nwatch, even under a standing FAIL. The phrase is the organ's only\noutput; a reason computed and not emitted is the c43 class\n(context computed then thrown away by the handler) wearing a\nseverity ladder.\